# Template only -- lists the variable names this stack's docker-compose.yml
# expects. Real values live in Infisical, never here and never in git.
# scripts/render-env.sh writes the actual .env next to this file on the host.
#
# This is the shared/central Postgres instance other stacks' apps connect
# to (as opposed to a stack that ships its own dedicated Postgres container,
# like Authentik or Infisical). It uses zero ${VAR} substitution in
# docker-compose.yml, and on purpose: it's the one stack in this repo that's
# already fully on the "right" pattern -- file-based Docker secrets instead
# of plain env vars for credentials. All three of its credentials come from
# ./secrets/*.txt files mounted via the top-level `secrets:` block, not from
# this .env file:
#
#   secrets/pg_user.txt        -> POSTGRES_USER_FILE (the postgres superuser)
#   secrets/pg_pw.txt          -> POSTGRES_PASSWORD_FILE (its password)
#   secrets/arcane_pg_pw.txt   -> a second secret Arcane itself reads to talk
#                                 to this Postgres (this stack just supplies
#                                 the file; Arcane's own DATABASE_URL wiring
#                                 lives over in the arcane stack).
#
# Those secrets/*.txt files are covered by the repo's .gitignore and are
# never committed -- create them by hand on the host before first start.
# Everything else here (POSTGRES_DB, TZ, PGTZ, tuning flags) is hardcoded
# directly in docker-compose.yml rather than templated, which is why it
# doesn't show up as a variable either.
